  "findings": [
    "Current ordinary 2026 diagram and after-revision PER are byte-identical to previously reviewed PDFs. Article 3.4 specifies 125 core plus 10 ITEC EC; Appendix 2 and the current elective page specify 50 elective EC, summing to 185. The same PER cohort diagram and ordinary curriculum diagram instead total 180 EC using 120 core. Article 3.4(8) requires at least 45 elective EC, without explaining Appendix 2. Current Committee Rules explicitly support 50 elective EC for 2023–2024 and later entrants but do not amend core volume. The complete pathway remains blocked pending authoritative reconciliation.",
    "The PER landing page explicitly applies AR to students starting in or after September 2023. No specialisations are defined; use the ordinary 2026 entrant diagram rather than the separate 2025 version. ELA is 25 EC within elective space and requires its relevant coach/PlanApp approval; DBID31 is a noncredit administrative code, and an internship is not universal.",
    "PER p82 requires 120 earned EC, compulsory Year 1, DPB240, DCB200, 3PHYS and DLB385 plus signed approval for the final project. The assessment table pp83–85 has additional course/elective conditions; the partial display is not a complete entry checklist. Project and PPD progression, three 5 EC PPD units, embedded MyFuture and five noncredit SG obligations remain verified. Appendix 3 pilots concern MyFuture, sustainability assessment and calculus assessment, without changing aggregate credit volume.",
    "All 59 exact-target rows were re-read and reconciled with current registry identifiers, interests and the 14 previously bounded discovery attributions. Eighteen generators retain unique provisional ownership in two coherent candidate directions; 27 support and 14 search/outcome rows retain their roles. Current official programme and major-course content supports their academic substance; application examples are not compulsory specialisations or additional qualifications.",
    "Actual consumer-product investigation, needs/specification work, prototyping and user inquiry connect substantively to intelligent systems through vision, learning, robotics, signals and responsible business/circularity. This is a meaningful programme-level response. Integrated aesthetic studio, extensive project-line and individual capstone correspondence is not assumed. Closest concept, additional distinct route and stopping judgments remain provisional while the external credit framework is unresolved; no final no-match."
  ],
  "officialAlternative": "Current Forms and Files and PER landing page distinguish the applicable after-revision curriculum and separate September 2025 cohort. Newly inspected current Examination Committee Regulations, p16, delegates PlanApp approval of 50 elective EC for 2023–2024 and later entrants. It corroborates the elective volume but provides no correction of the formal 125 core EC or explicit precedence resolving the aggregate. No individual exemption is presumed.",
  "searchBoundary": "Two targeted search engines supplied current course/assessment references but no applicable credit amendment. This negative search is not proof that an amendment does not exist. The explicit conflict in inspected current formal sources is the blocker, not an inaccessible source.",
  "remainingEssentialEvidence": "Reconcile the adopted2026-entrant Industrial Design credit framework: PER Art3.4(3)125core + Art3.4(5)10ITEC + Appendix2 p76/ordinarydiagram50elective =185, versus the same PER cohortdiagram p78 and current2026–27diagram120core+10ITEC+50elective=180. Art3.4(8)atleast45elective would close180 but Appendix2/guide require50. Need authoritative amendment, explicit precedence or reconciliation; do not silently subtract5 or combine cohorts.",
